# Decision tree



Agent routes from user intent **without requiring** a slash command unless the user wants the full skill ritual.



| User intent | First action |

|-------------|--------------|

| bug, error, stack trace, wrong data, flaky | Debug discipline ([`change-control-manifest.mdc`](../change-control-manifest.mdc) steps 1–4); `/debug` if user attached or non-trivial |

| copy, label, known small UI (outcome clear) | Direct minimal patch — **no** `/debug` mantra |

| new screen / mock / component architecture | `/builder-ui` |

| cross-layer / full-stack **feature** (UI+API+schema) | `/builder-feature` — **plan only**; implement via specialist per approved slice |

| review PR / plan | `/scrutinize` |

| database / SQL | `/builder-schema` |

| API contract, backend, REST, endpoint design | `/builder-api` |

| deploy, CI/CD, IaC, observability, infra | `/builder-infrastructure` |

| push / commit | `/git-push` — if several git roots in the workspace, `cd` the repo the user means first |

| mobile / native client bug (login, API error, crash) | Debug discipline in that **client repo** — **not** `/builder-feature` |

| improve skills in this repo | `/upgrade-ai` |

| RCA after **one** validated fix | `/fix-record` |

| one commit, multiple unrelated fixes | PR description or **one fix-record per root cause** — ask scope |

| unsure bug vs copy | One clarifying question, then row above |



If multiple apply, use the row for the **active mode**:



| Active mode | Sequence (skip steps that do not apply) |

|-------------|----------------------------------------|

| **Patch / fix** (default) | diagnose → patch → verify → git-push |

| **Plan-only** (`/builder-feature`) | plan phases → handoff — **no app patch** |

| **Read-only** (`/scrutinize` review-only) | review → report — **no patch** unless user approves fixes |

| **Meta upgrade** (`/upgrade-ai` on skills/rules) | diagnose → minimal skill/rule edit → verify — app patch sequence N/A |



When a skill with an **iron law** is active (e.g. plan-only, no app edits), that skill **overrides** patch steps 7–8 and conflicting routing for the turn.

